.TH PQBLOCKS 3 "2026-09-17" "pqblocks 1.0.0" "PQBlocks Library Manual"
.SH NAME
pqblocks \- Post-Quantum / Classical Hybrid Cryptographic CLI and Engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pqblocks
\fBkem keygen\fR \-\-out \fIfile.json\fR
.br
.B pqblocks
\fBkem encaps\fR \-\-in \fIkem.json\fR \-\-out \fIencaps.json\fR
.br
.B pqblocks
\fBkem decaps\fR \-\-in \fIencaps.json\fR \-\-out \fIshared.key\fR
.br
.B pqblocks
\fBsig keygen\fR \-\-out \fIsig.json\fR
.br
.B pqblocks
\fBsig sign\fR \-\-in \fIsig.json\fR \-\-msg \fImessage.txt\fR \-\-out \fIsig.bin\fR
.br
.B pqblocks
\fBsig verify\fR \-\-in \fIsig.json\fR \-\-msg \fImessage.txt\fR \-\-sig \fIsig.bin\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBpqblocks\fR is a quantum-inspired, classically executed hybrid cryptographic utility providing
dual-layer quantum resistance by combining classical primitives with post-quantum standards.
.PP
The KEM mechanism binds ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203) with X25519 (RFC 7748) via HKDF-SHA256 (RFC 5869)
and key confirmation (HMAC-SHA256).
.PP
The signature mechanism binds ML-DSA-65 (FIPS 204) with Ed25519 (RFC 8032) in a composite
structure per draft-ietf-lamps-pq-composite-sigs.
.SH ENVELOPE FORMAT
All JSON outputs include self-describing cryptographic envelopes specifying suite ID, algorithms,
and container lengths.
.SH RETURN VALUES
The CLI exits with 0 on success, or non-zero error codes corresponding to the PQBLOCKS error taxonomy.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pqblocks_hybrid (3),
.BR pqblocks_policy (5)
